  message: "SATISFIED via the minified-heuristic gate (supply_chain.py). ROOT CAUSE (corrected from the filing's 'signature length' framing): is_likely_minified() Heuristic 1 (avg line length >150) is language-agnostic, so a dense-but-real Python file — a data/lookup module, a very long function signature, generated protobuf without a @generated header — was classified tier-4 DERIVED and the default tier filter dropped its WHOLE file (0 nodes, no diagnostic). Fix: gate Heuristic 1 to _MINIFIABLE_WEB_EXTENSIONS (JS/CSS/HTML/TS/vue/svelte); the @generated/sourcemap/webpack heuristics stay universal. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (re-ran the item's own repro): a Python file with a 30-param signature (avg line >150) previously emitted 0 nodes for the whole file; now emits its symbols (test_dense_python_file_not_silently_dropped: 0->1 'wide' node). Self-corpus: scip_pb2.py stays DERIVED (via its 'DO NOT EDIT' header, Heuristic 3); _embedding_data.py (base64 blob, no header) correctly reclassified first-party (+5 variable nodes). smart-test 4092 passed / 100% cov. The generalized 'record tier-filtered drops in limits' honesty half is beyond this item's statement — filed as follow-up WI-tulit."  # 5ed0
